## Lore

The Kryygorth Pegasus, the K-Pegasus or K-Peg for short, is a beautiful winged creature very like the true Pegasus, with large majestic wings, deep blue eyes and a toned, muscular body. It could pass for the legendary creature but for its human-like forearms and articulated hands of two thick fingers and an opposable thumb. It runs on all fours but often stands and sits upright like a biped. It has human-like intelligence, a lovely singing voice and a little magic. Its origins are lost; it is believed to be another hybrid Bio-Wizard creation of the ancient Splugorth Lord Kryygorth.

K-Pegs are a huge attraction at the Splugorth Slave Market, and dwindling supply against high demand keeps their price rising. Buyers prefer them to flying animals because a K-Peg can become a trusted companion as well as a beast of burden. Those who like and respect their masters (or friends, if free) stand with them to the bitter end and let them and others ride. They are social by nature and work well with others; abused, they are hard to train and control, but they respond to kindness and patience. Most are white, pale grey, bluish white or bluish light grey; only 10% are dark grey and 5% black.

Free K-Pegs prefer plains and mountains but turn up anywhere. On Rifts Earth they are known in and around the Andes, the Himalayas and the Appalachian Mountains. They often ally with other peaceful creatures such as the Zembahk and the real Pegasus, and a few have joined the Liberated Underground to help others of their kind escape. Their enemies are the Splugorth, their minions and nearly every other evil creature.

## Value

A domesticated Kryygorth Pegasus (obedient and trustworthy) sells for 600,000+ credits. Wild or unmanageable ones sell for as little as 100,000 and are typically chained, their wings clipped, and put to hard labor.
